-- The same refusal as `export-refused.l4`, reached the other way: this @export
-- names the imported section GIVEN itself rather than a rule that reads it.
--
-- Worth its own fixture because the two go through different machinery. A rule
-- with a non-empty read-set is a DECIDE; the section GIVEN is elaborated to a
-- 0-ary ASSUME, which is never a read-set key, so an earlier build of the
-- refusal did not see this shape at all -- and because `the rate` carries a
-- TYPICALLY, that build answered a wrong number with "status":"success" rather
-- than failing. Found by an adversarial pass, 2026-09-08.

IMPORT `implicit-rate-lib`

@export What this amount comes to at the imported rate, named directly.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`straight cost of` amount MEANS amount TIMES `the rate`
